In the beginning, two rivers flowed from the same mountain spring—the River of Clear Waters and the River of Deep Currents. Each possessed magic: Clear Waters could reveal truth, while Deep Currents could multiply any gift cast into its flow threefold.

The rivers agreed to share their powers. Clear Waters would send portions of its essence to Deep Currents, trusting it would return enriched water to nourish the valleys below. In the first season, Clear Waters sent a small stream. Deep Currents, true to its nature, tripled it and returned half—more than was originally given. The valleys bloomed.

Encouraged, Clear Waters sent more in the second season. Deep Currents again returned generously, and prosperity spread across the land.

But in the third season, Deep Currents grew proud. "Why should I return what my power has multiplied?" it wondered. When Clear Waters sent its largest offering yet, Deep Currents kept nearly everything, returning only a trickle.

Clear Waters, betrayed, withdrew its trust and sent nothing more. Deep Currents, without new water to multiply, began to stagnate. Both rivers diminished, and the valleys withered.

